<details>
<summary>High-Level Assessment</summary>

<dl>
<dd>

<br/>

>The following are alternative approaches to this PR:

<details>
<summary><b>1. Structured tool-call protocol (no command parsing)</b></summary>

<dl>
<dd>

- ➕ Avoids ambiguous parsing of user text (e.g., accidental &#x27;!&#x27;)
- ➕ Easier to validate/authorize specific operations
- ➕ Aligns with typical agent tool-call schemas
- ➖ Requires frontend changes to send/receive structured tool intents
- ➖ More work than the current lightweight UX

</dd>
</dl>

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>2. Separate terminal endpoint usage (explicit UI action)</b></summary>

<dl>
<dd>

- ➕ Clear user intent and safer UX (click-to-run)
- ➕ Keeps chat endpoint focused on LLM responses
- ➖ Less convenient than inline &#x27;!cmd&#x27; messages
- ➖ More UI surface area to build/maintain

</dd>
</dl>

</details>

>**Recommendation:** Current approach is acceptable for a fast iteration, but consider moving toward a structured tool-call schema or an explicit terminal UI action to reduce ambiguity and improve safety/authorization over time.

</dd>
</dl>

</details>

